  </div>

  <section class="mb-16 border-t border-hairline pt-12">
    <h2 class="text-display-sm text-primary uppercase tracking-wider mb-8">F\u00F3rmulas & Exemplos Resolvidos</h2>

    <FormulaBox title="F\u00F3rmulas Matem\u00E1ticas">
      <p>
        O consumo di\u00E1rio \u00E9 a soma de todas as cargas dos aparelhos multiplicada pelas horas de uso:
      </p>
      <div class="bg-surface-soft p-4 font-mono text-primary border border-hairline my-2">
        Consumo Di\u00E1rio (Wh) = \u03A3 (Pot\u00EAncia do Aparelho \u00D7 Horas de Uso)
      </div>
      <p>
        A capacidade necess\u00E1ria considera limites de DoD e dura\u00E7\u00E3o do acampamento:
      </p>
      <div class="bg-surface-soft p-4 font-mono text-primary border border-hairline my-2">
        Capacidade (Ah) = (Consumo Di\u00E1rio \u00D7 Dias) / (DoD% \u00D7 Tens\u00E3o)
      </div>
      <p>
        Limites de DoD: LFP 80%, NMC 80%, Chumbo-\u00E1cido 50%.
      </p>
    </FormulaBox>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6 mt-8">
      <WorkedExample
        number={1}
        title="Camping de Fim de Semana \u2014 Geladeira, Luzes, Bomba d'\u00E1gua"
        scenario="Um casal vai a um parque estadual de acampamento para uma viagem de fim de semana. Eles precisam de energia para a geladeira, luzes LED e uma bomba d'\u00E1gua ao longo de 2 dias sem energia da rede."
        inputs={[
          { label: "Geladeira", value: "150W \u00D7 8h/dia" },
          { label: "Luzes LED", value: "40W \u00D7 6h/dia" },
          { label: "Bomba d'\u00E1gua", value: "60W \u00D7 1h/dia" },
          { label: "Tens\u00E3o do Sistema", value: "12V" },
          { label: "Qu\u00EDmica", value: "LFP (80% DoD)" },
          { label: "Dura\u00E7\u00E3o da Viagem", value: "2 dias" },
        ]}
        steps={[
          "Carga di\u00E1ria = (150\u00D78) + (40\u00D76) + (60\u00D71) = 1.200 + 240 + 60 = 1.500 Wh/dia",
          "Energia total da viagem = 1.500 Wh \u00D7 2 dias = 3.000 Wh",
          "Ah necess\u00E1rios = 3.000 / (0,80 \u00D7 12) = 312,5 Ah",
        ]}
        answer="Um banco de bateria LFP 12V 350 Ah (arredondado para tamanho pr\u00E1tico) fornece 4.200 Wh, cobrindo a necessidade de 3.000 Wh do fim de semana com uma reserva confort\u00E1vel."
        interpretation="Esta configura\u00E7\u00E3o deixa ~30% de reserva no final do segundo dia, acomodando cargas inesperadas ou um ciclo tardio da geladeira. Um banco LFP 350 Ah pesa cerca de 35 kg \u2014 gerenci\u00E1vel para a maioria dos caminhonetes de camping."
        variant="rv"
      />

      <WorkedExample
        number={2}
        title="Vida Permanente em RV \u2014 Cargas Extensivas com Solar"
        scenario="Um RVer que trabalha remotamente de um motorhome Classe C. O sistema inclui carregamento solar (pain\u00E9is de 400W) que suplementa a bateria durante o dia, reduzindo o armazenamento noturno necess\u00E1rio."
        inputs={[
          { label: "Geladeira", value: "80W \u00D7 12h/dia (ciclos do compressor)" },
          { label: "Laptop + Monitores", value: "200W \u00D7 8h/dia" },
          { label: "Ilumina\u00E7\u00E3o LED", value: "60W \u00D7 5h/dia" },
          { label: "Bomba d'\u00E1gua", value: "60W \u00D7 1h/dia" },
          { label: "Roteador + Starlink", value: "75W \u00D7 24h/dia" },
          { label: "Ventilador", value: "20W \u00D7 10h/dia" },
          { label: "Carregamento Celular/Tablet", value: "30W \u00D7 3h/dia" },
          { label: "Tens\u00E3o do Sistema", value: "12V" },
          { label: "Qu\u00EDmica", value: "LFP (80% DoD)" },
          { label: "Coleta Solar", value: "~1.600 Wh/dia (400W \u00D7 4 horas pico)" },
        ]}
        steps={[
          "Carga di\u00E1ria = (80\u00D712) + (200\u00D78) + (60\u00D75) + (60\u00D71) + (75\u00D724) + (20\u00D710) + (30\u00D73) = 960 + 1.600 + 300 + 60 + 1.800 + 200 + 90 = 5.010 Wh/dia",
          "Demanda noturna l\u00EDquida = 5.010 \u2212 1.600 (solar) = 3.410 Wh (solar cobre cargas diurnas)",
          "Ah necess\u00E1rios = 3.410 / (0,80 \u00D7 12) = 355,2 Ah",
          "Com reserva de 1 dia de autonomia: 3.410 \u00D7 2 / (0,80 \u00D7 12) = 710,4 Ah",
        ]}
        answer="Um banco de bateria LFP 12V 750 Ah fornece 9.000 Wh. Com 400W de solar reposto ~1.600 Wh/dia, o sistema alcan\u00E7a quase equil\u00EDbrio em dias ensolarados."
        interpretation="Vida permanente demanda um banco maior porque trabalho remoto torna voc\u00EA dependente de energia. A matriz solar \u00E9 cr\u00EDtica \u2014 sem ela, voc\u00EA precisaria de 1.100+ Ah. Em dias nublados, espere 40\u201360% de redu\u00E7\u00E3o solar, ent\u00E3o um gerador de backup \u00E9 recomendado."
        variant="rv"
      />

      <WorkedExample
        number={3}
        title="Boondocking Sem Solar \u2014 Maximize a Autonomia"
        scenario="Um boondocker em um caminhonete-camper quer 4 dias de completa independ\u00EAncia energ\u00E9tica sem solar, carregamento por alternador ou gerador. O objetivo \u00E9 maximizar o tempo off-grid antes de precisar dirigir para recarregar."
        inputs={[
          { label: "Geladeira Compressor 12V", value: "60W \u00D7 10h/dia (50% ciclo de trabalho)" },
          { label: "Luzes LED Puck", value: "20W \u00D7 5h/dia" },
          { label: "Bomba d'\u00E1gua", value: "50W \u00D7 0,5h/dia" },
          { label: "Carregamento de Dispositivos", value: "40W \u00D7 3h/dia" },
          { label: "Tens\u00E3o do Sistema", value: "12V" },
          { label: "Qu\u00EDmica", value: "LFP (80% DoD)" },
          { label: "Alvo de Autonomia", value: "4 dias" },
        ]}
        steps={[
          "Carga di\u00E1ria = (60\u00D710) + (20\u00D75) + (50\u00D70,5) + (40\u00D73) = 600 + 100 + 25 + 120 = 845 Wh/dia",
          "Energia total de 4 dias = 845 \u00D7 4 = 3.380 Wh",
          "Ah necess\u00E1rios = 3.380 / (0,80 \u00D7 12) = 352,1 Ah",
          "Tamanho pr\u00E1tico do banco: 400 Ah (arredonda para 4\u00D7100Ah m\u00F3dulos LFP padr\u00E3o)",
        ]}
        answer="Um banco de bateria LFP 12V 400 Ah (4.800 Wh) fornece 4 dias completos de energia com 1.420 Wh (29,6%) de reserva para emerg\u00EAncias."
        interpretation="Sem solar ou carregamento, cada Wh importa. Esta configura\u00E7\u00E3o assume uso disciplinado \u2014 sem cargas desperdi\u00E7adoras. Considere um painel solar dobr\u00E1vel de 200W como backup emergencial; mesmo sol parcial adiciona 200\u2013400 Wh/dia e estende a autonomia para 5\u20136 dias."
        variant="rv"
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <EngineeringDiagram
    title="Arquitetura do Sistema de Energia RV"
    description="Carregamento por alternador, entrada solar e armazenamento de bateria alimentando cargas de RV"
    variant="system"
    steps={[
      { label: "Alternador/Solar", icon: "solar" },
      { label: "Controlador de Carga", icon: "charge" },
      { label: "Banco de Baterias", icon: "battery" },
      { label: "Cargas do RV", icon: "load" },
    ]}
  />

  <ComparisonTable
    title="Comparativo de Qu\u00EDmicas de Bateria RV"
    headers={["Caracter\u00EDstica", "LiFePO4", "AGM Chumbo-\u00E1cido", "C\u00E9lula Gel"]}
    rows={[
      ["Peso (100Ah)", "12 kg", "30 kg", "28 kg"],
      ["Capacidade Utiliz\u00E1vel", "80\u201390 Ah", "50 Ah", "50 Ah"],
      ["Vida \u00FAtil", "5.000+", "500\u20131.000", "1.000"],
      ["Taxa de Carga", "0,5\u20131C", "0,1C", "0,1C"],
      ["Pre\u00E7o (100Ah 12V)", "R$4.000\u20136.000", "R$1.000\u20131.500", "R$1.250\u20131.750"],
      ["Autorrecarga", "1\u20133%/m\u00EAs", "3\u20135%/m\u00EAs", "2\u20134%/m\u00EAs"],
      ["Manuten\u00E7\u00E3o", "Nenhuma", "Verificar \u00E1gua", "Nenhuma"],
    ]}
    caption="LFP tem custo inicial maior, mas economia de ciclo de vida superior para uso em RV"
  />

  <FAQSection items={faqItems} />

  <script>
    import { calculateRVBattery } from '../../../utils/calculators';

    const applianceList = document.getElementById('appliance-list') as HTMLElement;
    const addApplianceBtn = document.getElementById('add-appliance') as HTMLButtonElement;
    const voltageInput = document.getElementById('voltage') as HTMLInputElement;
    const campingDays = document.getElementById('camping-days') as HTMLInputElement;
    const chemistrySelect = document.getElementById('chemistry') as HTMLSelectElement;

    const resultDailyBox = document.getElementById('result-daily');
    const resultDailyValue = resultDailyBox?.querySelector('.text-display-md') as HTMLElement;
    const resultDailyKwh = resultDailyBox?.querySelector('.text-caption') as HTMLElement;

    const resultCapacityBox = document.getElementById('result-capacity');
    const resultCapacityValue = resultCapacityBox?.querySelector('.text-title-lg') as HTMLElement;
    const resultCapacityRef = resultCapacityBox?.querySelector('.text-caption') as HTMLElement;

    const resultRecommendedBox = document.getElementById('result-recommended');
    const resultRecommendedValue = resultRecommendedBox?.querySelector('.text-title-lg') as HTMLElement;
    const resultRecommendedRef = resultRecommendedBox?.querySelector('.text-caption') as HTMLElement;

    const systemNotes = document.getElementById('system-notes');

    let rowIndex = 3;

    function createApplianceRow(index: number): HTMLElement {
      const row = document.createElement('div');
      row.className = 'appliance-row flex flex-col gap-3 p-3 bg-surface-soft border border-hairline rounded';
      row.dataset.index = String(index);
      row.innerHTML = `
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
          <span class="text-label-uppercase text-xs text-primary">Aparelho ${index + 1}</span>
          <button type="button" class="remove-row text-caption text-red-600 hover:text-red-400 cursor-pointer" aria-label="Remover linha do aparelho">\u2715</button>
        </div>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-3">
          <div class="flex flex-col gap-1">
            <label for="appliance-name-${index}" class="text-label-uppercase text-[10px] text-muted">Nome</label>
            <input id="appliance-name-${index}" type="text" class="text-input w-full" value="Novo Aparelho" aria-label="Nome do aparelho ${index + 1}" />
          </div>
          <div class="flex flex-col gap-1">
            <label for="appliance-power-${index}" class="text-label-uppercase text-[10px] text-muted">Pot\u00EAncia (W)</label>
            <input id="appliance-power-${index}" type="number" class="text-input w-full" value={0} min={0} step={10} aria-label="Pot\u00EAncia do aparelho ${index + 1} em watts" />
          </div>
          <div class="flex flex-col gap-1">
            <label for="appliance-hours-${index}" class="text-label-uppercase text-[10px] text-muted">Horas/dia</label>
            <input id="appliance-hours-${index}" type="number" class="text-input w-full" value={0} min={0} max={24} step={0.5} aria-label="Horas por dia do aparelho ${index + 1}" />
          </div>
        </div>
      `;
      return row;
    }

    function updateRemoveButtons() {
      const rows = applianceList.querySelectorAll('.appliance-row');
      const removeBtns = applianceList.querySelectorAll('.remove-row');
      removeBtns.forEach(btn => {
        if (rows.length <= 1) {
          (btn as HTMLElement).classList.add('hidden');
        } else {
          (btn as HTMLElement).classList.remove('hidden');
        }
      });
    }

    function updateCalculations() {
      const rows = applianceList.querySelectorAll('.appliance-row');
      const loads: number[] = [];
      const hours: number[] = [];

      rows.forEach(row => {
        const powerInput = row.querySelector('[id^="appliance-power-"]') as HTMLInputElement;
        const hoursInput = row.querySelector('[id^="appliance-hours-"]') as HTMLInputElement;
        loads.push(parseFloat(powerInput?.value) || 0);
        hours.push(parseFloat(hoursInput?.value) || 0);
      });

      const voltage = parseFloat(voltageInput.value) || 12;
      const days = parseFloat(campingDays.value) || 3;
      const chemistry = chemistrySelect.value as "lfp" | "nmc" | "lead-acid";

      const results = calculateRVBattery(loads, hours, voltage, days, chemistry);

      if (resultDailyValue) resultDailyValue.textContent = `${Math.round(results.dailyConsumptionWh).toLocaleString()} Wh`;
      if (resultDailyKwh) resultDailyKwh.textContent = `${(results.dailyConsumptionWh / 1000).toFixed(2)} kWh por dia`;

      if (resultCapacityValue) resultCapacityValue.textContent = `${results.requiredCapacityAh.toFixed(1)} Ah`;
      if (resultCapacityRef) resultCapacityRef.textContent = `A ${voltage}V nominal`;

      if (resultRecommendedValue) resultRecommendedValue.textContent = `${results.recommendedBankSizeAh} Ah`;
      if (resultRecommendedRef) resultRecommendedRef.textContent = `Arredondado para tamanho pr\u00E1tico`;

      if (systemNotes) {
        const chemistryName = chemistry === "lfp" ? "LFP" : chemistry === "nmc" ? "NMC" : "Chumbo-\u00E1cido";
        systemNotes.textContent = `Para ${days} dia${days > 1 ? 's' : ''} de boondocking com ${Math.round(results.dailyConsumptionWh).toLocaleString()} Wh de consumo di\u00E1rio a ${voltage}V ${chemistryName}, voc\u00EA precisa de um banco de bateria de ${results.recommendedBankSizeAh} Ah.`;
      }
    }

    addApplianceBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const row = createApplianceRow(rowIndex);
      applianceList.appendChild(row);
      rowIndex++;
      updateRemoveButtons();
      row.querySelectorAll('input').forEach(input => {
        input.addEventListener('input', updateCalculations);
      });
      row.querySelector('.remove-row')?.addEventListener('click', () => {
        row.remove();
        updateRemoveButtons();
        updateCalculations();
      });
      updateCalculations();
    });

    applianceList.querySelectorAll('.appliance-row').forEach(row => {
      row.querySelectorAll('input').forEach(input => {
        input.addEventListener('input', updateCalculations);
      });
      row.querySelector('.remove-row')?.addEventListener('click', () => {
        row.remove();
        updateRemoveButtons();
        updateCalculations();
      });
    });

    [voltageInput, campingDays, chemistrySelect].forEach(el => {
      el.addEventListener('input', updateCalculations);
    });

    updateRemoveButtons();
    updateCalculations();
  </script>

</CalculatorLayout>
